  <static seed="127" source="Library/UVA-Stew5e/setUVA-Stew5e-C03S05-ChainRule/3-5-55.pg">
    <statement><p>A table of values for <m>f</m>, <m>g</m>, <m>f'</m>, and <m>g'</m> is given below.
<me>\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|} \hline
 x \amp  f(x)\amp  g(x) \amp  f ' (x) \amp  g' (x) \\ \hline
1 \amp  1 \amp   3 \amp  3 \amp  3 \\ \hline
2 \amp  3 \amp  1 \amp  1 \amp  3 \\ \hline
3\amp  3 \amp  1 \amp  2 \amp  2  \\ \hline
\end{array}</me></p>
<p>(A) If <m>h(x)=f(g(x))</m>, then <m>h'(1)</m> = <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(B) If <m>H(x)=g(f(x))</m>, then <m>H'(1)</m> = <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>By the chain rule:
<me>h'(1)= f'(g(1)) \cdot g'(1) = f'(3) \cdot 3
= 2 \cdot 3  = 6</me>
<me>H'(1)= g'(f(1)) \cdot f'(1) = g'(1) \cdot 3
= 3 \cdot 3  = 9</me></p>
</solution>
